&lt;h2&gt;About us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://constructorlabs.org/&quot;&gt;Constructor Labs&lt;/a&gt; is the research arm of Constructor Knowledge, based at Campus Ring 1 in Bremen, Germany. Our work is organized around three units: Knowledge Labs, Cyber Labs and Science Labs. We apply computing, software and robotics research to make scientists, teachers and students more effective, working with institutional partners that include CERN, NUS, Carnegie Mellon and Fraunhofer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our &lt;a href=&quot;https://constructorlabs.org/solutions/edtech/&quot;&gt;EdTech practice&lt;/a&gt; produces research that runs in production. AI-supported remote proctoring is in use at the Irish Aviation Authority, Princess Nourah University and Saudi Electronic University, and our course delivery platform is used by CERN, EPFL, MariaDB and Acronis. For industry clients, we build tailored BSc, MSc and PhD pipelines, L&amp;amp;D operating models, AI upskilling programmes and customer training systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Constructor Labs Solutions (CLS)&lt;/strong&gt; is our client-facing systems integrator for the education and research sector, launching in September 2026. It brings audit and consultancy, content, platform, talent and R&amp;amp;D services together under a single contract, an offer few providers make to education buyers today. Delivery is orchestrated across several Constructor organizations: CUB, Nexford, Nexademy, EBAC, Constructor Labs and Constructor Tech. Our aim is to become the go-to systems integrator for education in EMEA by 2029.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will open EMEA markets for Constructor Labs Solutions as a quota-carrying individual contributor. The role rests on an established network among universities, online education providers, EdTech vendors and corporate L&amp;amp;D and research

&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;IMC is seeking Deep Learning Researchers to join our growing team. As a Deep Learning Researcher, you will develop and apply state-of-the-art deep learning techniques at the intersection of AI and markets. You will help accelerate our efforts in areas such as modern neural network architectures and representation learning, improving our large-scale AI models that increasingly shape our trading. You will work closely with senior researchers to gain exposure to the full research lifecycle, from initial idea to production deployment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;The ideal candidate has a strong foundation in modern AI and machine learning research, gained through post-graduate study or internships. Prior financial industry experience is not required. We are looking for someone who brings rigorous scientific thinking and a drive to learn, and who wants to grow alongside experienced researchers as we build a world-class deep learning capability at IMC.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Core Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and improve deep learning models to enhance trading performance across multiple asset classes, working under the guidance of senior researchers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Contribute to research in areas such as representation learning, transformers, foundation models, generative AI, reinforcement learning, and other emerging deep learning techniques&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Support large-scale data curation, feature representation, and self-supervised and multimodal learning from structured and unstructured datasets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Contribute to shared training infrastructure and deployment pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Stay current with academic and industry developments

&lt;p&gt;IMC is seeking a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Compensation Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to join our global Compensation team and play a key role in supporting the firm’s continued growth across Europe. Reporting to the Head of Compensation, this role will have regional responsibility for compensation across Europe and will lead critical initiatives spanning job architecture, pay structures, benchmarking, and annual compensation processes. The role will sit within a global team and will be responsible for global strategic projects and processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a strategic partner, you will collaborate with business leaders, HR, and cross-functional teams to design and deliver compensation programs that are market-competitive, internally equitable, and aligned with IMC’s global rewards philosophy and local regulatory requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
